name: Internal settings and capped heuristic preserve honest partial work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/internal_tool_limits.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: options uaf-hunt:hunt
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 Alloc free pairs | structured-option
keys: Enter C-u
require-live-snap: 25 EDIT Alloc free pairs | opened-structured-editor
paste-file: @ART/pairs.txt
require-live-snap: 25 owned_alloc | structured-editor
resize: 160x48
live-snap: editor-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: editor-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: editor-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: editor-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: editor-40x12
expect: save session
ask: Is the advanced JSON draft readable and editable across six sizes, with clear session and global save controls and no work starting?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-g
require-live-snap: 25 Saved globally. | stored-option
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/internal_tool_limits.py @TMP_TARGET @ART options
submit: options chrome-rce:scan
require-live-snap: 25 Experimental | experimental-scan
submit: logs
submit: run chrome-rce:scan {"maxFindings":1}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/internal_tool_limits.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
paste-file: @ART/partial-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · partial | capped-receipt
expect: Finding limit 1 reached
resize: 160x48
live-snap: partial-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: partial-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: partial-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: partial-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: partial-40x12
expect: partial
keys: NPage
live-snap: partial-cause-40x12
expect: inspected
ask: Across six sizes, can the operator read the partial outcome and reach the finding-limit cause without interpreting the comment-only signal as a verified vulnerability?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | review-signal
expect: broker/owned.cc
submit: decision deferred Owned inert heuristic signal needs owner review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/internal_tool_limits.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Finding review completeness does not describe repository coverage. | report-limits
expect: REPORT
expect: 1 finding
resize: 160x48
live-snap: report-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: report-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: report-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: report-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: report-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: report-reading-40x12
ask: Across six sizes, does Report keep the recorded deferral separate from repository coverage without treating a reached finding limit as complete inspection?
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | json-format
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/internal_tool_limits.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: show advanced uaf-hunt:hunt
require-live-snap: 25 owned_alloc | recovered-option
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/partial-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · partial | recovered-partial
expect: Finding limit 1 reached
keys: Escape
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | recovered-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/internal_tool_limits.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the structured setting, one partial heuristic observation and its deferral with no UAF scan, model request or target execution?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
